  "id": "phonological-recoding",
  "term": "phonological recoding",
  "definition": "Phonological recoding is the automatic, usually unconscious conversion of a written word’s spelling into its sound-based form in the mind. It supports identifying words during silent reading and is considered an important part of skilled reading.",
